<<if !$CompletedQuests.includes("Ben: Track Meet Cute")>>
    You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> about his opinions on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> and he gives you a strange look. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He is… unique.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> replies, taking a minute to decide on the word. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I mean, super friendly, but he… How do I put this? He’s hard to be around, for me, at least. Plus, he’s always interrupting class and if I get sat next to him it is IMPOSSIBLE to focus!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> sighs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Despite that, it’s hard to dislike him. He’s just… a lot.”</span>
<<else>>
    You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> about his opinions on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> and he ponders for a moment before replying. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He is a lot. I mean, I don’t dislike the kid, but we are polar opposites. I want a nice class where we can learn and practice our skills and he wants a playground. He started jumping around in class the other day and just… ugh…”</span> You laugh, it makes sense that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span>’s wildest antics would cause the studious and nerdy <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> to get frustrated. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But he is also one of the nicest people ever! So, it’s hard to be mad at him for stuff.”</span>
<</if>><br>
<br>
<<endByLocation>>

