    You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> about his opinions on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>? He’s alright. Little scary, but aren’t all rich people?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> talks about him very nonchalantly, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I don’t really talk to him at all, but we went to this special lunch during the last week of school last year, since we tied for the highest grade. He was super nice and even bought me a soda. So yeah, I like him.”</span>
<<else>>
    You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> about his opinions on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> and he smiles. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He’s super nice. Like, you’d think rich people would be full of themselves or scary… well, I guess he kind of is, but in a nice way.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> talks about him genuinely, <span style="color:Yellow">surprising you since <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> always seems so intimidating.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We’ve only really hung around each other at school functions, since we tend to be the two with the highest grades, but he’s always been super nice to me. I think we’d get along, but I understand that we live in different social groups.”</span>
<</if>><br>
